1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
Why can hard calcium stop a stent opening
fully?

2
00:00:04,156 --> 00:00:08,185
Calcium in the artery wall can make a
narrowed section stiff.

3
00:00:08,626 --> 00:00:13,259
In this example, part of the stent stays
tight as the surrounding section

4
00:00:13,328 --> 00:00:14,083
opens.

5
00:00:14,687 --> 00:00:18,692
Calcium can build up within the plaque in
a coronary artery.

6
00:00:19,203 --> 00:00:23,487
Its location, length, and spread around
the wall vary.

7
00:00:23,998 --> 00:00:26,912
An angiogram can sometimes show calcium.

8
00:00:27,353 --> 00:00:32,531
A scan from inside the artery, using
ultrasound or OCT, can help the

9
00:00:32,578 --> 00:00:35,469
team work out how much of the wall is
affected.

10
00:00:36,166 --> 00:00:39,707
A stent is designed to open and support
the treated section.

11
00:00:40,403 --> 00:00:44,525
If a stiff area prevents it from opening
sufficiently, the channel can remain

12
00:00:44,641 --> 00:00:49,772
narrow. When the team expects that
problem, it may prepare the lesion before

13
00:00:49,819 --> 00:00:54,892
placing a stent. The purpose is to make
the narrowed section easier to

14
00:00:54,973 --> 00:00:55,902
expand.

15
00:00:56,703 --> 00:00:59,536
One option is a specialised balloon.

16
00:01:00,128 --> 00:01:03,658
Some have scoring elements or small
cutting elements.

17
00:01:04,354 --> 00:01:09,463
These concentrate force against selected
areas of plaque as the balloon opens.

18
00:01:10,276 --> 00:01:14,745
The team chooses a method based on the
calcium and whether the device can reach

19
00:01:14,815 --> 00:01:16,174
the narrowed section.

20
00:01:16,777 --> 00:01:19,970
Another option is intravascular
lithotripsy.

21
00:01:20,481 --> 00:01:24,451
A balloon-based device delivers pulses
that create pressure waves.

22
00:01:25,148 --> 00:01:29,838
In selected lesions those waves can
fracture calcium within the wall, making

23
00:01:29,885 --> 00:01:32,160
it easier for the vessel to expand.

24
00:01:32,764 --> 00:01:36,688
In this illustration you can see fine
cracks forming in the calcium.

25
00:01:37,385 --> 00:01:40,311
Atherectomy is a different type of
preparation.

26
00:01:40,915 --> 00:01:45,536
Some systems use a small rotating element
to modify hard plaque.

27
00:01:46,046 --> 00:01:50,238
The anatomy and the risks of the procedure
guide that decision.

28
00:01:50,934 --> 00:01:55,485
This scene shows a separate example of an
option the team may choose.

29
00:01:56,089 --> 00:01:59,804
After suitable preparation, the team may
place a stent.

30
00:02:00,408 --> 00:02:05,040
It checks the final result using the
angiogram and may use an inside-artery

31
00:02:05,098 --> 00:02:08,651
scan to look at expansion and contact with
the wall.

32
00:02:09,255 --> 00:02:14,235
The practical aim is a well-expanded stent
and a satisfactory blood-flow result in

33
00:02:14,282 --> 00:02:15,745
the treated artery.
